# What `gcloud builds submit` uploads to the Cloud Build source bucket.
#
# gcloud reads THIS file, not .dockerignore. Without it, gcloud falls back to a
# .gitignore-derived default, which still shipped a 62.9 MiB / 426-file tarball
# because local build output was swept in. Keep the two lists roughly in sync
# with .dockerignore, but remember they serve different stages: this one governs
# what leaves your machine, .dockerignore governs what the daemon sees.

# Dependencies and build output — reinstalled/rebuilt inside the image
node_modules
.next
out
build
dist

# Secrets. .env.example is documentation and carries no values; everything else
# is excluded so it never reaches the source bucket.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# VCS and tooling metadata
.git
.gitignore
.github
.vscode
.idea

# Tests, fixtures and QA output — not needed to build or serve
tests
coverage
playwright-report
test-results
*.log

# Docs and working artifacts
*.md
!README.md
artifacts
docs

# Schema tooling caches — the committed schema is what is used
.schema-introspection

# OS noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
